From fc017748633375f366d841f346bbbc33b2e91cc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artyom Shalkhakov <artyom.shalkhakov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:11:55 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Show a nib-loaded scroll view's document from its origin

A scroll view loaded from a xib can open scrolled away from its
document's origin, by however much the decoding moved the document.

The clip view puts its document at the origin when it is decoded and
leaves its bounds at zero; then the scroll view tiles, the clip view
takes the size the theme gives it, and a document that is pinned to the
top (flexibleMinY, as Interface Builder sets it) moves with the clip
view's edge. The bounds stay where they were, so the visible rect no
longer starts at the document's origin. Our default theme's scrollers
are wider than the ones the xib was laid out for, so even a scroll view
exactly as Interface Builder wrote it opens a few points down; one whose
clip view the xib gives another height than its scroll view has room
for (RDLDesigner's canvas) opens more than an inch down.

AppKit ends nib instantiation with -[NSScrollView setDocumentView:],
which scrolls the clip view to the document's frame origin, whatever
bounds the nib held (seen with a breakpoint on -setBoundsOrigin: of a
clip view subclass on macOS 15): after loading, the clip view's bounds
origin is the document's frame origin and the visible rect starts at
the document's origin, flipped or not. Do the same once the decoded
scroll view has tiled.

Tests/gui/NSScrollView/nibDocumentOrigin.m loads DocumentOrigin.xib, a
window with two scroll views laid out as Interface Builder writes them,
one with an unflipped document and one with a flipped one. Its checks
hold on macOS 15 for the same xib compiled with ibtool; without the
change four of them fail here (the clip view's bounds origin stays at
zero while the document has moved 6 points), with it all pass. The
other NSScrollView and NSClipView tests still pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/NSScrollView.m                      |  4 +
 Tests/gui/NSScrollView/DocumentOrigin.xib  | 67 +++++++++++++++
 Tests/gui/NSScrollView/nibDocumentOrigin.m | 95 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 166 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Tests/gui/NSScrollView/DocumentOrigin.xib
 create mode 100644 Tests/gui/NSScrollView/nibDocumentOrigin.m

diff --git a/Source/NSScrollView.m b/Source/NSScrollView.m
index 7f71dbfe9..608150e62 100644
--- a/Source/NSScrollView.m
+++ b/Source/NSScrollView.m
@@ -1660,6 +1660,10 @@ - (id) initWithCoder: (NSCoder*)aDecoder
       // set the document view into the content.
       [self setContentView: content];
       [self tile];
+      if (docView != nil)
+        {
+          [content setBoundsOrigin: [docView frame].origin];
+        }
       // Reenable notification sending.
       [docView setPostsFrameChangedNotifications: post_frame];
       [docView setPostsBoundsChangedNotifications: post_bound];
